r concern - insufficient duration\n\n**5. Energy:**\nDaily totals (resting + active):\n- 5/13: 1,731 + 303 = 2,034 kcal\n- 5/14: 1,223 + 1,531 = 2,754 kcal (high activity day - badminton)\n- 5/15: 1,215 + 437 = 1,651 kcal\n- 5/16: 1,728 + 1,498 = 3,226 kcal (high activity - badminton)\n- 5/17: 1,727 + 326 = 2,053 kcal\n- 5/18: 1,728 + 341 = 2,069 kcal\n- 5/19: 76 + 1 = 77 kcal (incomplete)\n\n**6. Workouts:**\n- 5/14: Badminton 1h56min, 1,104 kcal, avg HR 158, peak 193\n- 5/16: Badminton 2h35min, 1,253 kcal, avg HR 146, peak 181\n- Both sessions: high intensity, Z4+Z5 dominant, slow recovery\n\n**7. Nutrition:**\n- No nutrition records at all!\n\nNow let me create a comprehensive analysis.\n\nKey findings:\n1. Sleep deprivation is serious - only 4.5h sleep on 5/17, no proper night sleep on 5/18\n2. Step counts are decent on most days (6,500-12,000)\n3. High-intensity badminton twice a week with high heart rates\n4. No nutrition tracking\n5. Medical conditions: vestibular vertigo and conjunctivitis\n6. Three active medications\n7. Heart rate recovery is slow after exercise - potential concern\n8. The resting heart rate during sleep was quite low (~49-56 bpm) which could be normal for fit individuals\n\nLet me present this in a well-organized manner."}, "kind": "deepThought"}, {"id": "BAA790DC-9925-4D46-8DA8-4D506225CD41", "created_at": "2026-05-18T17:28:23.000Z", "updated_at": "2026-05-18T17:34:40.000Z", "deep_thought_card": {"reasoning_duration_ms": 376485, "reasoning_visibility": "full", "reasoning_expanded": false, "reasoning_content": "Let me compile a comprehensive analysis for 赵道凯 based on all the data I've gathered. Let me organize this by category.\n\n**1. Health Conditions:**\n- 前庭性眩晕 (Vestibular vertigo) - diagnosed 2025-08-02 at 苏州大学附属第四医院 神经内科\n- 结膜炎 (Conjunctivitis) - diagnosed 2026-04-20 at 苏州大学附属第四医院 皮肤科\n\n**2. Medications:**\n- 盐酸氮卓斯汀滴眼液 (Azelastine HCl eye drops) - 1 drop, 2x/day\n- 普拉洛芬滴眼液 (Pranoprofen eye drops) - 1 drop, 4x/day\n- 甲磺酸倍他司汀片 (Betahistine mesilate) - 6mg, 3x/day\n\n**3. Steps (May 13-19):**\n- 5/13: 6,587 steps, 4.18 km\n- 5/14: 12,100 steps, 8.12 km\n- 5/15: 9,168 steps, 6.49 km\n- 5/16: 9,641 steps, 6.52 km\n- 5/17: 10,129 steps, 6.31 km\n- 5/18: 4,684 steps, 3.12 km\n- 5/19: 10 steps (only early morning data)\n- Weekly total: 52,319 steps, 34.74 km\n- Daily average (excluding 5/19): ~8,718 steps/day\n\n**4. Sleep:**\n- 5/17: 4h37min total, 4h28min sleep - very short! REM 59min, Deep 32min, Core 2h57min\n- 5/18: Only 1h nap at 19:00 - essentially no proper night sleep\n- Sleep is a major concern - insufficient duration\n\n**5. Energy:**\nDaily totals (resting + active):\n- 5/13: 1,731 + 303 = 2,034 kcal\n- 5/14: 1,223 + 1,531 = 2,754 kcal (high activity day - badminton)\n- 5/15: 1,215 + 437 = 1,651 kcal\n- 5/16: 1,728 + 1,498 = 3,226 kcal (high activity - badminton)\n- 5/17: 1,727 + 326 = 2,053 kcal\n- 5/18: 1,728 + 341 = 2,069 kcal\n- 5/19: 76 + 1 = 77 kcal (incomplete)\n\n**6. Workouts:**\n- 5/14: Badminton 1h56min, 1,104 kcal, avg HR 158, peak 193\n- 5/16: Badminton 2h35min, 1,253 kcal, avg HR 146, peak 181\n- Both sessions: high intensity, Z4+Z5 dominant, slow recovery\n\n**7. Nutrition:**\n- No nutrition records at all!\n\nNow let me create a comprehensive analysis.\n\nKey findings:\n1. Sleep deprivation is serious - only 4.5h sleep on 5/17, no proper night sleep on 5/18\n2. Step counts are decent on most days (6,500-12,000)\n3. High-intensity badminton twice a week with high heart rates\n4. No nutrition tracking\n5. Medical conditions: vestibular vertigo and conjunctivitis\n6. Three active medications\n7. Heart rate recovery is slow after exercise - potential concern\n8. The resting heart rate during sleep was quite low (~49-56 bpm) which could be normal for fit individuals\n\nLet me present this in a well-organized manner."}, "kind": "deepThought"}, {"id": "05FECE8C-B16B-47D4-B472-8AA626CC8DDC", "created_at": "2026-05-18T17:28:27.000Z", "updated_at": "2026-05-18T17:28:28.000Z", "text"